  "metadata": {
    "title": "Wintermute Enters Prediction Markets as Event Contract Trading Tops $60B",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "Wintermute is moving into prediction markets as a liquidity provider, adding one of crypto's largest trading firms to a sector that is quickly being pulled toward institutional market structure.\nThe London-based firm said it is now quoting two-sided markets on event contracts across leading venues, bringing automated liquidity to products that let traders price outcomes across politics, economics, sports, weather and other real-world events. The entry comes as event-contract trading has topped $60 billion in 2026, with major venues now processing more than $20 billion in monthly volume.\nWintermute already handles more than $3.5 trillion in annual trading volume across more than 70 exchanges, giving the firm a market-making base that prediction platforms have been trying to attract as they move beyond retail speculation. Benzinga reported that Wintermute averages more than $10 billion in daily trading volume across spot and derivatives crypto markets.\nMore From Cryptoprowl:\n-\nEightco Secures $125 Million Investment From Bitmine And ARK Invest, Shares Surge\n-\nStanley Druckenmiller Says Stablecoins Could Reshape Global Finance\nJake Ostrovskis, Wintermute's head of OTC trading, said prediction markets have \"the demand profile of a major asset class\" but still carry the liquidity profile of an early-stage market.\nThat gap is becoming the central story. Event contracts have gained attention as a way to trade real-world probabilities, but shallow order books can make large trades difficult without moving prices. Continuous bid and offer quoting is designed to narrow spreads, absorb larger directional flow and make market-implied probabilities more reliable for traders watching these contracts as live information signals.\nWintermute's timing also fits a broader institutional push. Kalshi recently raised $1 billion at a $22 billion valuation, while institutional trading volume on its platform has climbed sharply over the past six months. Robinhood (NASDAQ: $HOOD), ICE (NYSE: $ICE), Coinbase (NASDAQ: $COIN) and other financial firms have also been moving closer to the category.\nFor prediction markets, Wintermute's arrival adds another sign that event contracts are being treated less like a niche crypto product and more like an emerging trading venue for information, risk and liquidity.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "Wintermute is moving into prediction markets as a liquidity provider, adding one of crypto's largest trading firms to a sector that is quickly being pulled toward institutional market structure.",
      "The London-based firm said it is now quoting two-sided markets on event contracts across leading venues, bringing automated liquidity to products that let traders price outcomes across politics, economics, sports, weather and other real-world events. The entry comes as event-contract trading has topped $60 billion in 2026, with major venues now processing more than $20 billion in monthly volume.",
      "Wintermute already handles more than $3.5 trillion in annual trading volume across more than 70 exchanges, giving the firm a market-making base that prediction platforms have been trying to attract as they move beyond retail speculation. Benzinga reported that Wintermute averages more than $10 billion in daily trading volume across spot and derivatives crypto markets.",
      "More From Cryptoprowl:",
      "-",
      "Eightco Secures $125 Million Investment From Bitmine And ARK Invest, Shares Surge",
      "-",
      "Stanley Druckenmiller Says Stablecoins Could Reshape Global Finance",
      "Jake Ostrovskis, Wintermute's head of OTC trading, said prediction markets have \"the demand profile of a major asset class\" but still carry the liquidity profile of an early-stage market.",
      "That gap is becoming the central story. Event contracts have gained attention as a way to trade real-world probabilities, but shallow order books can make large trades difficult without moving prices. Continuous bid and offer quoting is designed to narrow spreads, absorb larger directional flow and make market-implied probabilities more reliable for traders watching these contracts as live information signals.",
      "Wintermute's timing also fits a broader institutional push. Kalshi recently raised $1 billion at a $22 billion valuation, while institutional trading volume on its platform has climbed sharply over the past six months. Robinhood (NASDAQ: $HOOD), ICE (NYSE: $ICE), Coinbase (NASDAQ: $COIN) and other financial firms have also been moving closer to the category.",
      "For prediction markets, Wintermute's arrival adds another sign that event contracts are being treated less like a niche crypto product and more like an emerging trading venue for information, risk and liquidity."
